If any character is suited for nethack's "rogue" role, it's Brand of
"Chronicles of Amber" fame, a psycho who wanted an Amulet of Yend -
oops, Jewel of Judgement - above anything else, shot his brother's
horse out from under him with a crossbow, teleported around in fights,
paralyzed people and then stabbed them in the back, you get the
picture.

What's more, this Brand ascended with his *worst enemy's sword in
hand*: Grayswandir, and got it by betraying his god with a HoOA. Heh
heh heh.

(Hey, Brand's technically dead, but maybe this is his pattern ghost
set on retrieving the Amulet and attaining independence. Don't worry
if you have no ***king clue what I just wrote...)

Many, many Brands met their doom in the dungeons because at first I
was very, very bad with flimsy rogues. Brand bones littered the
floors. A Brand priest even tamed a mummy of a previous Brand. Sadly,
that Brand met his doom on the 13th due to Spork updates. Oh well.
This Brand, at any rate, made it.

Telegraphic summary:
1. found blessed magic lamp, turned in for +3 blue dragon mail. Got it
at +3. Best wish ever; speed, shock resist (for killing priests) and
tremendous AC.
2. Delved for luckstone. Found two-handed sword in process, which
served as main weapon for long time.
3. Found bunch of crap in main dungeon, including scroll of genocide
and unid'd helm.
4. Nurse-danced in Sokoban; up to 174 HP.
5. Sword rusted and corroded; got spare from Rogue level (heh), which
was conveniently +2.
6. About to kill Minetown priest, since no other altar found (*never*
found one, heh!), but realized I had helm of opposite alignment and
the lawful gods had Grayswandir. Sacfested for 5000 turns, got
Snickersnee, Sunsword, some random piece of artifact poop, and a
silver saber named -

- Werebane. Oh well, useful for rogue quest due to poly control
(didn't use it :) ).

7. Finally got Grayswandir. Awesome! In gratitude, didn't kill stupid
priest. During sacfest, got wish from smoky potions of blindness;
traded for +3 cloak of magic resist.
8. Cleared castle with attack wands, Grayswandir, and conflict.
Conflict alone didn't due it due to low (11) CHA stat.
9. Cleared most of valley, found GoP, jumping boots at castle. Damn, I
loved the freedom having an amulet of reflection, BlDSM, and cloak of
magic resist gave for hats and boots. And jumping, speed at the same
time? Damn that rocked on Astral.
10. Wished for magic marker. Due to wands of polymorph being awesome,
barely used until ascension run. And damn did I need it back then.
10.5 Reduced to 6 HP while fighting Asmodeus due to summoning storm.
Thankfully, wearing "LS at time, but intrinsic speed saved life and
didn't need it.
11. BLAH BLAH Gehennom BLAH BLAH -
"You stuff yourself and then vomit voluminously. You can move again."
Oh my god, almost choked on a wraith corpse near start of ascension
run. Would have been worst death *ever*.
12. Killed Rodney. Switched from #twoweaponing +7 Grayswandir and +7
silver saber to shield of reflection, since killing no longer
priority. AC of -41 (with painstakingly polypiled shirt) meant
ascension run mostly a bother.
13. Astral! Rev. geno'd purple worms, which weren't much help due to
the huge AC boost of high-level monsters. Unfortunately, had no light
source, but thankfully several spare wands of light literally saved my
life.

Jumping and speed rule. Period. Second altar was Kos's; didn't need to
use helm of opposite alignment.
Now Brand really *is* a demigod, watch out universe!



